 ## Background
-The problem of regularization in NeRF optimization emerged from the observation that standard photometric loss alone leads to degenerate solutions, such as "floaters" (semi-transparent geometry) and poor generalization in sparse-view scenarios [7381-diffusion-regularized-nerf-training.md, 7475-geometric-baseline-regularization.md]. Early work like RegNeRF [8582-regnerf.md] introduced normalizing flows and smoothness priors to constrain the MLP output distribution. Subsequent methods like Geometric Baseline Regularization [7475-geometric-baseline-regularization.md] focused on explicit geometric constraints derived from ray weights. More recently, diffusion models [7381-diffusion-regularized-nerf-training.md] and adaptive frequency alignment [10454-adaptive-rendering-loss-regularization.md] have been employed to provide stronger priors for few-shot learning. These techniques are widely used in novel view synthesis, particularly in applications with limited input views such as cultural heritage documentation, autonomous driving, and robotics.
-
+The use of regularization in NeRF optimization emerged as a response to the limitations of standard photometric loss in sparse-view and ill-posed scenarios. Early works like RegNeRF introduced normalizing flows and smoothness priors to prevent MLP overfitting [S1]. Subsequent research explored geometric constraints, such as the Geometric Baseline Regularization which enforces foreground completeness and frustum consistency [7475-geometric-baseline-regularization.md]. More recent approaches have integrated generative priors, such as Diffusion-Regularized NeRF Training, which uses DDMs to regularize RGBD patches [7381-diffusion-regularized-nerf-training.md], and adaptive strategies like AR-NeRF which align positional encoding frequencies with rendering loss [10454-adaptive-rendering-loss-regularization.md]. These methods are widely used in novel view synthesis, especially for sparse inputs, misaligned captures, or large-scale distributed training [S1, 7381-diffusion-regularized-nerf-training.md, 10377-nerf-xl-multi-gpu-distortion-loss.md].
